From cdf63598869d1741754b243802cfef7d9bf700eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:44:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 45/45] Copy a Store to the guest unless this device reads the
 surface

With the changes before this one iconservicesagent on macOS 27.2 drew
its icons and still logged "Flattened representation is seemingly a
fully transparent image" for all 19. It draws each icon into a 104x104
IOSurface and reads the surface back with the CPU. The draw log showed
the pass store (resident_surface_store) and, when the guest unmapped the
surface 40 s later, writes=1: the pass's opening clear was the only
thing this device ever wrote to its pages.

The lazy rail keeps a Store in the host image until the guest names the
resource in CmdSynchronizeResources. For an IOSurface the guest sends
none: on Apple's host the attachment is the surface's own memory, so
there is nothing to ask for. The debt was paid only when the ledger
evicted it.

A Store now stays in the host image only for a surface this device has
itself read since the guest mapped it: one a draw sampled, a window
backing the compositor reads, or one the display presented. Any other is
copied to the guest's pages at once, as with REIMS_VGPU_LAZY_WRITEBACK=off.
A window backing pays one copy for its first frame.

After it, with the guest's icon caches cleared at boot, 13 of the 19
application icons in the Dock of a pulled 27.2 drew, one of them as a
black square; with the rail left as it was
none did, and with it switched off by hand the one icon redrawn in that
run did.

Tests: a Store into a surface this device has not read is not deferred,
and is once a draw has sampled the surface.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
